  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This private compatibility module only declares the legacy resource and\n selector address shapes; it has no handwritten executable code. Its derived\n serialization and identity operations do not emit source-line measurements.\n The source-tool argument and delivery regressions in `agent/tests.rs`\n exercise these addresses through the legacy adapter. Supported path-based\n address construction is tested separately in `tests/outline_content.rs`."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/resource.rs` (root) is a file-root coverage exception. It is written as fenced citation commentary in the file's inner doc comment, which the built-in allows. The citation is also allowed even though `OutlineId` is `#[cfg(test)]`.\n\nThe commentary is substantive and agrees with the current source:\n- **No handwritten executable code.** The file has only two structs, `ResourceId` and `OutlineId`, with derived `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize`. It has no function bodies.\n- **Legacy adapter tests.** The `agent/tests.rs` tests construct and consume these addresses through the legacy source-tool adapter. `source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads` and `source_reads_track_optional_dependencies_and_empty_searches_remain_discovery` use `ResourceId` and `OutlineId`, and `SourceSession::dispatch` in `agent/sources.rs` deserializes `ResourceId` and builds `OutlineId` from the tool arguments.\n- **Path-based address tests.** The supported path-based `crate::outline::OutlineId` is tested separately in `tests/outline_content.rs`, in `addresses_reconstruct_without_reading_the_file`, and in `tests/search.rs`. The commentary's claim about that split is accurate.\n\nThe two `{impl}` references in the file are to `requirements.sdk.sources.source_addresses`. They are not to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant with an `{impl}` or `{test}`. No gap found.",
